{:edb/db-before-t 2686 :edb/db-after-t 2687 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535999 50 #inst "2026-10-09T12:35:53.856Z" 13194139535999 true] [17592186105386 1100 "Find a vector equation of the straight line passing through $P(3,-1,7)$ and parallel to ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/assets/48f9afd751f6424fe465e494fd254593de065563231a1f5df07741789969c1af.png)" 13194139535999 true] [17592186105386 1100 "Find a vector equation of the straight line passing through $P(3,-1,7)$ and parallel to $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139535999 false] [17592186105386 1145 "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $P$ and parallel to $\\mathbf{v}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{p} + t \\mathbf{v},\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty, \\infty)$ and $\\mathbf{p}$ is the position vector of $P$.\n\nIn our case, the position vector of the point $P$ is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073156/assets/9264ecd5e62e51eec08ae686461f8b3d99aadbddd2363b5c700c72839d59524f.png)\n\nUsing the formula for the vector equation of a line, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535999 true] [17592186105386 1145 "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $P$ and parallel to $\\mathbf{v}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{p} + t \\mathbf{v},\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty, \\infty)$ and $\\mathbf{p}$ is the position vector of $P$.\n\nIn our case, the position vector of the point $P$ is $[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]$\n\nUsing the formula for the vector equation of a line, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535999 false] [17592186105821 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378834 13194139535999 true] [17592186105821 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378890 13194139535999 true] [17592186105821 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378903 13194139535999 true] [17592186105822 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378841 13194139535999 true] [17592186105822 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378883 13194139535999 true] [17592186105822 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378916 13194139535999 true] [17592186105823 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378848 13194139535999 true] [17592186105823 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378923 13194139535999 true] [17592186105824 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378855 13194139535999 true] [17592186105824 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378862 13194139535999 true] [17592186105824 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378869 13194139535999 true] [17592186105824 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378876 13194139535999 true] [17592186106213 1017 #edb/ref 17592186103787 13194139535999 false] [17592186106213 1017 #edb/ref 17592186378897 13194139535999 true] [17592186106213 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535999 true] [17592186106213 1100 "Find a vector equation of the straight line passing through $P(-1,-4, 5)$ and parallel to $v = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139535999 false] [17592186106213 1100 "Find a vector equation of the straight line passing through $P(-1,-4,5)$ and parallel to $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535999 true] [17592186106213 1145 "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $P$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=p+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nIn our case, the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nUsing the formula for the vector equation of a line, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535999 true] [17592186106214 1017 #edb/ref 17592186103793 13194139535999 false] [17592186106214 1017 #edb/ref 17592186378910 13194139535999 true] [17592186106214 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535999 true] [17592186106214 1100 "Find a vector equation of the line that passes through the points $A(4, 5, 3)$ and $B(-1, 2, 0)$." 13194139535999 false] [17592186106214 1100 "Find a vector equation of the line that passes through the points $A(4,5,3)$ and $B(-1,2,0).$" 13194139535999 true] [17592186106214 1145 "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $A$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=a+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $a$ is the position vector of $A.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $A(4,5,3)$ and $B(-1,2,0)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{AB} \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,0⟩-⟨4,5,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,-3,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378834 1017 #edb/ref 17592186378835 13194139535999 true] [17592186378834 1089 "q-126431" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378834 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535999 true] [17592186378834 1100 "Find a vector equation of the straight line passing through $Q(\\sqrt{5},\\,\\frac{3}{5},\\,-2)$ and parallel to $v=⟨2,\\,3,\\,-1⟩.$" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378834 1113 #uuid "00ffce9f-fde5-5943-bf47-164dc6539869" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378834 1145 "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $Q$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=q+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $q$ is the position vector of $Q.$ \n\nIn our case, the position vector of the point $Q$ is $q=⟨\\sqrt{5},\\,\\frac{3}{5},\\,-2⟩.$ \n\nUsing the formula for the vector equation of a line, we have\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\sqrt{5},\\,\\frac{3}{5},\\,-2⟩+t⟨2,\\,3,\\,-1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378836 13194139535999 true] [17592186378835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378837 13194139535999 true] [17592186378835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378838 13194139535999 true] [17592186378835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378839 13194139535999 true] [17592186378835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378840 13194139535999 true] [17592186378835 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535999 true] [17592186378835 1041 "selection" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378835 1104 #edb/ref 17592186378840 13194139535999 true] [17592186378835 1110 #uuid "feadbeec-0f45-58e5-9409-a37ec90ff75a" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378836 1034 "r=⟨-2,\\,\\frac{3}{5},\\,\\sqrt{5}⟩+t⟨-1,\\,2,\\,3⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378836 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535999 true] [17592186378836 1111 #uuid "c7fba8fc-77d6-5766-8fe9-f9d1c3909258" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378837 1034 "r=⟨2,\\,3,\\,-1⟩+⟨\\sqrt{5},\\,\\frac{3}{5},\\,-2⟩" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378837 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535999 true] [17592186378837 1111 #uuid "d01e8e91-d5f8-5ea6-8602-fea3c6efd8a2" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378838 1034 "r=⟨2,\\,3,\\,-1⟩+t⟨\\sqrt{5},\\,\\frac{3}{5},\\,-2⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378838 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535999 true] [17592186378838 1111 #uuid "184822ad-2e01-53b7-8688-5547d3e59400" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378839 1034 "r=⟨2,\\,-1,\\,3⟩+t⟨\\sqrt{5},\\,-2,\\,\\frac{3}{5}⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378839 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535999 true] [17592186378839 1111 #uuid "c58db8d9-9b95-50a8-a9e5-6ef7e09038fd" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378840 1034 "r=⟨\\sqrt{5},\\,\\frac{3}{5},\\,-2⟩+t⟨2,\\,3,\\,-1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378840 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535999 true] [17592186378840 1111 #uuid "608641f9-afb3-5bae-9d25-2a26c115ebb4" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378841 1017 #edb/ref 17592186378842 13194139535999 true] [17592186378841 1089 "q-126752" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378841 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535999 true] [17592186378841 1100 "Find a vector equation of the line that passes through the points $P(0,1,3)$ and $Q(3,-4,-2).$" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378841 1113 #uuid "d1a0662d-e8a7-5875-9a37-6a8d79742ba6" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378841 1145 "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $P$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=p+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $P(0,1,3)$ and $Q(3,-4,-2)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =⟨3,-4,-2⟩-⟨0,1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-5,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378842 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378843 13194139535999 true] [17592186378842 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378844 13194139535999 true] [17592186378842 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378845 13194139535999 true] [17592186378842 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378846 13194139535999 true] [17592186378842 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378847 13194139535999 true] [17592186378842 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535999 true] [17592186378842 1041 "selection" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378842 1104 #edb/ref 17592186378844 13194139535999 true] [17592186378842 1110 #uuid "ebf6e9b5-2957-558f-b65c-afc7fc8c7781" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378843 1034 "r=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378843 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535999 true] [17592186378843 1111 #uuid "86fb47a6-9951-5289-a89d-51470953df6b" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378844 1034 "r=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378844 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535999 true] [17592186378844 1111 #uuid "29ff2373-e25a-5d6b-afc4-878204b60ffd" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378845 1034 "r=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378845 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535999 true] [17592186378845 1111 #uuid "0379a423-f0ae-5fe9-9c4c-3f97e5d9dfe9" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378846 1034 "r=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378846 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535999 true] [17592186378846 1111 #uuid "495a29d4-4685-53f5-aa7e-aca0f6ac95c8" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378847 1034 "r=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378847 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535999 true] [17592186378847 1111 #uuid "6d50ad2d-de44-5bce-ac91-07540c84fecb" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378848 1017 #edb/ref 17592186378849 13194139535999 true] [17592186378848 1089 "q-126991" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378848 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535999 true] [17592186378848 1100 "Consider the straight line that passes through $P(3,1,1)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨-1,0,2⟩.$ Find all the possible points $A$ on that line such that $AP=\\sqrt{5}.$" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378848 1113 #uuid "9cdad390-9975-5637-84b8-1dc45af58338" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378848 1145 "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨3,1,1⟩+t⟨-1,0,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSince $A$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OA} & =⟨3,1,1⟩+t⟨-1,0,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PA} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨3,1,1⟩+t⟨-1,0,2⟩)-⟨3,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,⟨-1,0,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PA=\\sqrt{5},$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AP & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PA}| & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ |⟨-t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩| & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{(-t)^{2}+(0)^{2}+(2t)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{{t}^{2}+0+4{t}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5{t}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\pm \\sqrt{5}t & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ t & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 1$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{1}}=⟨3,1,1⟩+⟨-1,0,2⟩=⟨2,1,3⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{2}}=⟨3,1,1⟩-⟨-1,0,2⟩=⟨4,1,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are ${A}_{1}(2,1,3)$ and ${A}_{2}(4,1,-1).$" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378849 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378850 13194139535999 true] [17592186378849 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378851 13194139535999 true] [17592186378849 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378852 13194139535999 true] [17592186378849 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378853 13194139535999 true] [17592186378849 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378854 13194139535999 true] [17592186378849 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535999 true] [17592186378849 1041 "selection" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378849 1104 #edb/ref 17592186378852 13194139535999 true] [17592186378849 1110 #uuid "4744e544-4c7a-5dd4-ab0a-09c5f18432cc" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378850 1034 "${A}_{1}(2,1,-2)$ and ${A}_{2}(4,1,1)$" 13194139535999 true] [17592186378850 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535999 true] [17592186378850 1111 #uuid "0f43cf15-1614-5176-91fd-0190558ca9f9" 13194139535999 true] 